---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalNav from '../components/LegalNav.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../config/site';

const description =
  'Appidge privacy policy: no cookies or tracking on this site; rules and traffic stay on your Mac; license activation processes only the minimum required data, and payment data is handled by Creem, the Merchant of Record.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description={description} path="/privacy" locale="en">
  <div class="doc">
    <div class="container doc-layout">
      <LegalNav locale="en" current="privacy" />
      <article class="prose doc-main">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <div class="doc-meta">
        <span><b>Effective</b> 2026-07-24</span>
        <span><b>Last updated</b> 2026-07-24</span>
        <span><b>Covers</b> the appidge.com website and the Appidge macOS app</span>
      </div>

      <p class="lede">
        In one sentence: <strong>this site doesn't track you, the app's rules and traffic stay
        on your Mac, and we process only the minimum needed to activate a license.</strong>
      </p>

      <h2><span class="num">1</span>What this website collects</h2>
      <p>
        appidge.com is a fully static site: <strong>no cookies, no third-party tracking
        scripts, no profiling</strong>. Our hosting provider (Cloudflare) may briefly process
        access logs (such as IP addresses) under its own policies to serve and protect the
        site; we do not use those logs to identify or track individuals.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="num">2</span>Who handles your data at checkout</h2>
      <p>
        Purchases go through <strong>Creem</strong>'s hosted checkout. Creem is the
        <strong>Merchant of Record</strong> for this product: your name, email, payment
        details, billing address, and tax-related information are collected and processed by
        Creem as the transacting party, under
        <a href="https://www.creem.io/privacy" rel="noopener">Creem's privacy notice</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        We <strong>never see or store your card details</strong>. For delivery and support we
        may receive order-related essentials from Creem (order number, purchase email, license
        status).
      </p>

      <h2><span class="num">3</span>License activation and validation</h2>
      <p>
        When activating or periodically validating a license, Appidge sends our licensing
        service only what the check requires:
      </p>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>License key</td>
              <td>Verify the purchase</td>
              <td>Recorded server-side in redacted form; used for nothing else</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Install identifier</td>
              <td>Count activated devices</td>
              <td>
                A privacy-friendly random identifier — <strong>not</strong> your email, real
                hostname, or hardware serial number
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>App version</td>
              <td>Compatibility</td>
              <td>—</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        On your Mac, license data (key, install identifier, last validation time) lives in the
        <strong>macOS Keychain</strong> — never in plain text files.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="num">4</span>Data inside the app</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Your rule configuration, the list of intercepted processes, and connection details
          stay local — <strong>never uploaded to us</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Your network traffic is forwarded locally to the proxy you configured, or directly —
          <strong>it never passes through our servers</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          There is no built-in crash reporting or usage analytics. If that ever changes, it
          will be opt-in and this policy will be updated first.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2><span class="num">5</span>Update checks</h2>
      <p>
        The app periodically asks our update server for new versions. The request returns
        update information and contains nothing that identifies you personally; server access
        logs are handled as in section 1. Automatic checks can be turned off in the app's
        settings.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="num">6</span>Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        Server-side license records are kept while the license is active, to keep validation
        working. After a refund or deactivation, we retain the minimum needed to prevent abuse
        and meet legal obligations — for <strong>no more than 12 months</strong>, after which
        records are deleted or anonymized.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="num">7</span>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under applicable law you may request access to, correction of, or deletion of data we
        hold about you — email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
        Requests concerning payment data (invoices, billing details) may also need to go to
        Creem; we'll help you get connected.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="num">8</span>Contact and changes</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions: <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a><br />
        Data controller / operator: Appidge is run by an independent solo developer, reachable
        directly at the address above. For payment data, the controller is Creem.
      </p>
      <p>Material changes to this policy will be posted here with a new effective date.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
